.TH CVECTOR_RESET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_reset \- clear all elements and reset capacity
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

void cvector_reset(cvec v);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes every element from the vector. It then tries to shrink the
capacity back to the minimum of 4 elements. The capacity stays the same
when the reallocation fails. The element count still becomes 0.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v    Vector to reset
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The element count becomes 0
The capacity goes back to the minimum (4) when the reallocation
succeeds
Does not free the elements one by one. The caller must do this first
when it is necessary
Asserts if v is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_reset (3),
.BR cvector_destroy (3)
